1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,250
A car dashboard shows a few numbers that matter: speed, fuel, warnings. A business dashboard should do the same.

2
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:15,750
Pick three to five key numbers, each compared with last period or a target.

3
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:25,325
A good KPI connects to money or customers, changes with your actions, and is easy to understand.

4
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:32,820
Revenue, gross margin, returning customers and stock cover are common choices for a shop.

5
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:37,755
Too many KPIs means no focus. Pick a few.

6
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:45,775
Put the most important numbers at the top, trends below, and details at the bottom.

7
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:51,680
A number without a comparison means nothing. Always show against what.

